.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt OPENSSL-LIST 1ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm openssl-list
.Nd list algorithms and features
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm openssl list
.Oo
.Fl help ]
.Oo
.Fl verbose ]
.Oo
.Fl select
.Em name ]
.Oo
.Fl 1 ]
.Oo
.Fl all-algorithms ]
.Oo
.Fl commands ]
.Oo
.Fl standard-commands ]
.Oo
.Fl digest-algorithms ]
.Oo
.Fl digest-commands ]
.Oo
.Fl kdf-algorithms ]
.Oo
.Fl mac-algorithms ]
.Oo
.Fl random-instances ]
.Oo
.Fl random-generators ]
.Oo
.Fl cipher-algorithms ]
.Oo
.Fl cipher-commands ]
.Oo
.Fl encoders ]
.Oo
.Fl decoders ]
.Oo
.Fl key-managers ]
.Oo
.Fl skey-managers ]
.Oo
.Fl key-exchange-algorithms ]
.Oo
.Fl kem-algorithms ]
.Oo
.Fl tls-groups ]
.Oo
.Fl all-tls-groups ]
.Oo
.Fl tls1_2 ]
.Oo
.Fl tls1_3 ]
.Oo
.Fl signature-algorithms ]
.Oo
.Fl tls-signature-algorithms ]
.Oo
.Fl asymcipher-algorithms ]
.Oo
.Fl public-key-algorithms ]
.Oo
.Fl public-key-methods ]
.Oo
.Fl store-loaders ]
.Oo
.Fl providers ]
.Oo
.Fl engines ]
.Oo
.Fl disabled ]
.Oo
.Fl objects ]
.Oo
.Fl options
.Em command ]
.Oo
.Fl provider
.Em name ]
.Oo
.Fl provider-path
.Em path ]
.Oo
.Fl provparam
.Em [name:]key=value ]
.Oo
.Fl propquery
.Em propq ]
.Sh DESCRIPTION
This command is used to generate list of algorithms or disabled
features.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy -help
Display a usage message.
.It Sy -verbose
Displays extra information.
The options below where verbosity applies say a bit more about what that
means.
.It Sy -select Em name
Only list algorithms that match this name.
.It Sy -1
List the commands, digest-commands, or cipher-commands in a single
column.
If used, this option must be given first.
.It Sy -all-algorithms
Display lists of all algorithms.
These include:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Asymmetric ciphers
.It Decoders
.It Digests
.It Encoders
.It Key derivation algorithms (KDF)
.It Key encapsulation methods (KEM)
.It Key exchange algorithms (KEX)
.It Key managers
.It Symmetric key managers
.It Message authentication code algorithms (MAC)
.It Random number generators (RNG, DRBG)
.It Signature algorithms
.It Store loaders
.It Symmetric ciphers
.El
.It Sy -commands
Display a list of standard commands.
.It Sy -standard-commands
List of standard commands.
.It Sy -digest-commands
This option is deprecated.
Use
.Sy digest-algorithms
instead.
.Pp
Display a list of message digest commands, which are typically used as
input to the
.Xr openssl-dgst 1
or
.Xr openssl-speed 1
commands.
.It Sy -cipher-commands
This option is deprecated.
Use
.Sy cipher-algorithms
instead.
.Pp
Display a list of cipher commands, which are typically used as input to
the
.Xr openssl-enc 1
or
.Xr openssl-speed 1
commands.
.It Sy -cipher-algorithms Ns , Sy -digest-algorithms Ns , Sy -kdf-algorithms Ns , Sy -mac-algorithms ,
Display a list of symmetric cipher, digest, kdf and mac algorithms.
See
.Sx Display of algorithm names
for a description of how names are displayed.
.Pp
In verbose mode, the algorithms provided by a provider will get
additional information on what parameters each implementation supports.
.It Sy -random-instances
List the primary, public and private random number generator details.
.It Sy -random-generators
Display a list of random number generators.
See
.Sx Display of algorithm names
for a description of how names are displayed.
.It Sy -encoders
Display a list of encoders.
See
.Sx Display of algorithm names
for a description of how names are displayed.
.Pp
In verbose mode, the algorithms provided by a provider will get
additional information on what parameters each implementation supports.
.It Sy -decoders
Display a list of decoders.
See
.Sx Display of algorithm names
for a description of how names are displayed.
.Pp
In verbose mode, the algorithms provided by a provider will get
additional information on what parameters each implementation supports.
.It Sy -public-key-algorithms
Display a list of public key algorithms, with each algorithm as a block
of multiple lines, all but the first are indented.
The options
.Sy key-exchange-algorithms ,
.Sy kem-algorithms ,
.Sy signature-algorithms ,
and
.Sy asymcipher-algorithms
will display similar info.
.It Sy -public-key-methods
Display a list of public key methods.
.It Sy -key-managers
Display a list of key managers.
.It Sy -skey-managers
Display a list of symmetric key managers.
.It Sy -key-exchange-algorithms
Display a list of key exchange algorithms.
.It Sy -kem-algorithms
Display a list of key encapsulation algorithms.
.It Sy -tls-groups
Display a list of the IANA names of all available (implemented) TLS
groups.
By default the listed groups are those compatible with TLS 1.3.
.It Sy -all-tls-groups
Display a list of the names of all available (implemented) TLS groups,
including any aliases.
Some groups are known under multiple names, for example,
.Sy secp256r1
is also known as
.Sy P-256 .
By default the listed groups are those compatible with TLS 1.3.
.It Sy -tls1_2
When listing TLS groups, list those compatible with TLS 1.2
.It Sy -tls1_3
When listing TLS groups, output those compatible with TLS 1.3. TLS 1.3
is the current default protocol version, but the default version is
subject to change, so best to specify the version explicitly.
.It Sy -signature-algorithms
Display a list of signature algorithms.
.It Sy -tls-signature-algorithms
Display the list of signature algorithms available for TLS handshakes
made available by all currently active providers.
The output format is colon delimited in a form directly usable in
.Xr SSL_CONF_cmd 3
specifying SignatureAlgorithms.
.It Sy -asymcipher-algorithms
Display a list of asymmetric cipher algorithms.
.It Sy -store-loaders
Display a list of store loaders.
.It Sy -providers
Display a list of all loaded providers with their names, version and
status.
.Pp
In verbose mode, the full version and all provider parameters will
additionally be displayed.
.It Sy -engines
This option is deprecated.
.Pp
Display a list of loaded engines.
.It Sy -disabled
Display a list of disabled features, those that were compiled out of the
installation.
.It Sy -objects
Display a list of built in objects, i.e.
OIDs with names.
They're listed in the format described in
.Xr config 5 .
.It Sy -options Em command
Output a two-column list of the options accepted by the specified
.Em command .
The first is the option name, and the second is a one-character
indication of what type of parameter it takes, if any.
This is an internal option, used for checking that the documentation is
complete.
.It Sy -provider Em name
.It Sy -provider-path Em path
.It Sy -provparam Em [name:]key=value
.It Sy -propquery Em propq
See
.Xr openssl 1 ,
.Xr provider 7 ,
and
.Xr property 7 .
.El
.Ss Display of algorithm names
Algorithm names may be displayed in one of two manners:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Legacy implementations
Legacy implementations will simply display the main name of the
algorithm on a line of its own, or in the form
.Qo Li <foo Qc
bar>> to show that
.Qo Li foo Qc
is an alias for the main name,
.Qo Li bar Qc
.It Provided implementations
Implementations from a provider are displayed like this if the
implementation is labeled with a single name:
.Bd -literal
 foo @ bar
.Ed
.Pp
or like this if it's labeled with multiple names:
.Bd -literal
 { foo1, foo2 } @bar
.Ed
.Pp
In both cases,
.Qo Li bar Qc
is the name of the provider.
.El
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Sy -engines ,
.Sy -digest-commands ,
and
.Sy -cipher-commands
options were deprecated in OpenSSL 3.0.
.Pp
The
.Sy -skey-managers
option was added in OpenSSL 3.5.
